github.com/owlnewworlds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T21:44:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T21:44:16Z","body":"> [@owlnewworlds](https://github.com/owlnewworlds) Godot probably doesn't add this metadata. There might be any other plugin that's also adding this metadata.\n\nI do add the metadata myself but it always works. The plugin creator wonders if I wouldn't have two plugins in my project. I dont think it's possible but since I'm using a dev Godot build, maybe I would need to clean some directories or what ?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2998031351/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2998049443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107912#issuecomment-2998049443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107912","id":2998049443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yspqj","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-23T21:50:11Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T21:50:11Z","body":"Did you replace your `res://android/build` folder with the source template from 4.5 beta 1?\nRemember that \"Install Android Build Template\" needs to be run for any engine version change.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2998049443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2998977534","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107912#issuecomment-2998977534","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107912","id":2998977534,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ywMP-","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T06:24:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T06:24:05Z","body":"> > [@owlnewworlds](https://github.com/owlnewworlds) Godot probably doesn't add this metadata. There might be any other plugin that's also adding this metadata.\n> \n> I do add the metadata myself but it always works. The plugin creator wonders if I wouldn't have two plugins in my project. I dont think it's possible but since I'm using a dev Godot build, maybe I would need to clean some directories or what ?\n\nThe error you're seeing is a manifest merge conflict, not something specific to Godot itself. I doubt that it works in `4.4.1.stable` but fails in `4.5.beta1`, this behavior is determined by the Android Gradle Plugin, not the Godot editor.\n\nYou can’t have two <meta-data> tags with the same `android:name` but different `android:value` Gradle will throw an error unless you explicitly tell it which one to use. To fix this, you need to add `tools:replace=\"android:value\"` to your <meta-data> tag so it overrides the value from the library.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2998977534/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999061524","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107912#issuecomment-2999061524","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107912","id":2999061524,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ywgwU","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T06:56:55Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T06:58:00Z","body":"> Not reproducible with Godot 4.4.1 stable\n\n@owlnewworlds To verify this, I tested using the sample plugin from\n[https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Plugin-Template](https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Plugin-Template) and it's also reproducible in `4.4.1.stable`.\n\n**Steps to Reproduce:**\n\n1. In the plugin’s [manifest](https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Plugin-Template/blob/main/plugin/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml), I added the following `<meta-data>` entry and built the plugin ([GodotAndroidPluginTemplate.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20877498/GodotAndroidPluginTemplate.zip)).\n\n ```xml\n <meta-data\n     android:name=\"org.godotengine.metadata.test\"\n     android:value=\"xxxxxxxxxx\"/>\n ```\n\n2. Opened a new project in `Godot 4.4.1.stable` and added the plugin.\n\n3. Enabled the plugin in `Project Settings` and installed the Android build template.\n\n4. In the project-level manifest `[project]/android/build/AndroidManifest.xml`, I added a conflicting `<meta-data>` tag:\n\n ```xml\n <meta-data\n     android:name=\"org.godotengine.metadata.test\"\n     android:value=\"yyyyyyyyyy\"/>\n ```\n\n5. Exported the project.\n\n**Result**:\n- A manifest merge conflict occurs, which confirms this issue also affects `4.4.1.stable`, not a regression in `4.5`.\n\n**Note:** This is the expected behavior of the Android Gradle manifest merger. When two <meta-data> entries with the same name but different value are found, it throws merge error and you must resolve the conflict manually. In this case:\n```xml\n<meta-data\n    android:name=\"org.godotengine.metadata.test\"\n    android:value=\"yyyyyyyyyy\"\n    tools:replace=\"android:value\" />\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999061524/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999356035","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107912#issuecomment-2999356035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107912","id":2999356035,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yxoqD","user":{"login":"owlnewworlds","id":156072785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCU17UQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/156072785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds","html_url":"https://github.com/owlnewworlds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owlnewworlds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T08:36:09Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T08:36:09Z","body":"> > Not reproducible with Godot 4.4.1 stable\n> \n> [@owlnewworlds](https://github.com/owlnewworlds) To verify this, I tested using the sample plugin from https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Plugin-Template and it's also reproducible in `4.4.1.stable`.\n> \n> **Steps to Reproduce:**\n> \n> 1. In the plugin’s [manifest](https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Plugin-Template/blob/main/plugin/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml), I added the following `<meta-data>` entry and built the plugin ([GodotAndroidPluginTemplate.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20877498/GodotAndroidPluginTemplate.zip)).\n> \n> <meta-data\n>     android:name=\"org.godotengine.metadata.test\"\n>     android:value=\"xxxxxxxxxx\"/>\n> 2. Opened a new project in `Godot 4.4.1.stable` and added the plugin.\n> 3. Enabled the plugin in `Project Settings` and installed the Android build template.\n> 4. In the project-level manifest `[project]/android/build/AndroidManifest.xml`, I added a conflicting `<meta-data>` tag:\n> \n> <meta-data\n>     android:name=\"org.godotengine.metadata.test\"\n>     android:value=\"yyyyyyyyyy\"/>\n> 5. Exported the project.\n> \n> **Result**:\n> \n> * A manifest merge conflict occurs, which confirms this issue also affects `4.4.1.stable`, not a regression in `4.5`.\n> \n> **Note:** This is the expected behavior of the Android Gradle manifest merger. When two entries with the same name but different value are found, it throws merge error and you must resolve the conflict manually. In this case:\n> \n> <meta-data\n>     android:name=\"org.godotengine.metadata.test\"\n>     android:value=\"yyyyyyyyyy\"\n>     tools:replace=\"android:value\" />\n\nThat's weird because I've never had the issue before. But well, ok, I'll see with the plugin creator what's going on.\nThank you!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999356035/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]